  "summary": {
    "en": "Two Cameroonians were reported killed while serving in Russia's army, and the African Bar Association has called for mediation in Cameroon, while the UN Human Rights Committee released findings on the country. Agbor Balla reflected on a decade of bloodshed in the Anglophone crisis, and questions are being raised about when children can safely return to school. The conflict recorded 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
